---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Myofascial Release | Nikki Leonardi Bodywork Traverse City" description="Myofascial release for the tension you can feel but can't quite touch. Traverse City therapeutic massage specialist.">
  <div class="pt-16">
    <section class="py-24 px-6 bg-[#162040]">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="section-label mb-4">Myofascial Release</p>
        <h1 class="font-['Playfair_Display'] text-5xl text-[#f0f4ff] leading-tight mb-6">The tension you can feel<br/>but can't quite touch —<br/><em class="text-[#c8a84b]">that's usually fascia.</em></h1>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="py-20 px-6 bg-[#0d1428]">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-[#c8a84b]/70 leading-relaxed text-lg">
        <p>Fascia is the connective tissue that surrounds every muscle, bone, nerve, and organ in your body. When it gets restricted — through injury, repetitive motion, or just how you've been moving — it creates patterns of tension that don't respond to pressure the way muscle does.</p>
        <p>Myofascial release works with those patterns directly. It's slower and more specific than deep tissue. It's often what unlocks the thing that nothing else has touched.</p>
        <p>If you've been to multiple therapists and can't shake a persistent issue — there's a good chance the fascial component hasn't been addressed yet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-12">
        <a href="/book" class="btn-primary">Book a Session</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
